The fix is applied. Here's what changed:

**Bug:** Line 7 used `b.url === inc.url` — a raw string comparison that is case-sensitive. Hostname case differences (`example.com` vs `EXAMPLE.com`) were not recognized as duplicates, so the incoming bookmark was appended as a second entry instead of being merged.

**Fix:** Import `normalizeUrl` from `url_utils.ts` and compare `normalizeUrl(b.url) === normalizeUrl(inc.url)` instead. `normalizeUrl` lowercases the hostname, so URLs that differ only in hostname case are now correctly treated as the same bookmark and merged (tags unioned).

The lint error about `.ts` extensions is pre-existing (requires `allowImportingTsExtensions` in tsconfig) and not introduced by this edit.


